      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"screaming\" or high-pitched noise at higher boost levels can be attributed to the compressor impeller blades, particularly the rotor and their vanes, which move at very high speeds. When the turbine spins the compressor at a high RPM, the impeller blades catch on air swirls and turbulence, creating a sound that's often compared to a scream or a high-pitched yell. This is due to the acceleration of the air through the impeller, which creates a region of low-pressure and high-velocity flow.",
